<title>GERMANY: German cabinet approves Waigel's 1998 tax bill.</title>
<headline>German cabinet approves Waigel's 1998 tax bill.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German cabinet on Tuesday approved Finance Minister Theo Waigel's 1998 tax bill, which would introduce the first phase of a coalition package of 30 billion marks in tax cuts, a government spokesman said.</p>
<p>The measure would lop two points off the 7.5 percent solidarity surcharge next year, as well as making initial cuts in corporate and commercial income taxes.</p>
</text>
